[00:41.25]Hiding it unspoken — how fragile your eyes are
[00:51.25]Eyes turning red — you liked me once, and that's enough
[01:03.55]Counting down the tenderness, the clock ticks on — don't take back the kiss
[01:19.35]One gust and I scatter — yet you caught me
[01:31.35]Wandering through a lonely heart — lovers, or friends
[01:45.05]Love needs no reason, like a kite that longs for the sky
[01:57.05]Maybe you understand me
[02:03.55]Love is an hourglass — grip it tight and it still slips away
[02:14.20]In the classroom corner, embracing — a hidden love like sparks
[02:27.90]Whispered at my ear: stay and love me
[02:38.20]A paper plane traces an unfinished dream — your name is still in my hand